<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><documents xmlns:xsi = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation = "HDocumentSchema.xsd"><document type = "H"><pnldref>H17208</pnldref><english><title>Aid and abet / assist in the fraudulent mutilation of a stamp with intent</title><additionalkeywords><additionalkeyword>aid and abet</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>aided and abetted</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>assisted</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>fraud</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>fraudulently</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>mutilate</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>mutilated</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>stamp</additionalkeyword></additionalkeywords><standardoffencewording>On **(..SPECIFY DATE..) at **(..SPECIFY TOWNSHIP..) knowingly aided, abetted or assisted **(..SPECIFY PERSON..) to fraudulently mutilate a stamp, with intent that use should be made of any part of that stamp</standardoffencewording><legislation>Contrary to section 13(1), (2) and (5) of the Stamp Duties Management Act 1891.</legislation><pointstoprove>date and location&lt;br /&gt;knowingly aided and abetted/assisted in the&lt;br /&gt;fraudulent&lt;br /&gt;mutilation of a stamp&lt;br /&gt;with intent that some use would be made &lt;br /&gt;of any part of the stamp</pointstoprove><investigatoractions><investigatoraction><code>IA1</code><description>Fingerprint and photograph</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA2</code><description>DNA Samples: If crime scene stain present - take evidential sample If no crime scene stain and DNA not confirmed on PNC - take Criminal Justice sample. If DNA confirmed on PNC - CJ sample not required</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA27</code><description>Confirm proposed charge is appropriately authorised (Police or CPS)</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA28</code><description>Ensure compliance with investigator's obligations re disclosure</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA29</code><description>Consider if case suitable for referral to Financial Investigation Unit and CPS for asset recovery eg confiscation order</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA3</code><description>Audio record interview unless exempt</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA4</code><description>PNC recordable</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA5</code><description>Submit a crime report</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA6</code><description>Offences brought to justice scheme</description></investigatoraction></investigatoractions><policeandcpschargingresponsibilities>D27968</policeandcpschargingresponsibilities></english><indictment><indictmentindicator><code>N</code><description>No</description></indictmentindicator><structuredindictmentindicator><code>N</code><description>No</description></structuredindictmentindicator></indictment><other><powersofarrest>Arrest without warrant</powersofarrest><modeoftrial><code>EWAY</code><description>EITHER WAY</description></modeoftrial><timelimitforprosecutions>None</timelimitforprosecutions><penalty>Summary: Six months imprisonment and / or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.&lt;br /&gt;Indictment: Ten years imprisonment and / or a fine.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Time limit for prosecutions:&lt;br /&gt;None&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;On the 12th March 2015 the limit on fines imposed by a Magistrates' court was removed – as such, the potential fine on summary conviction in relation to an offence committed after this date is unlimited.</penalty><geographicregion><code>EW</code><description>England and Wales</description></geographicregion></other><codes><cjsoffencecode>SD91010</cjsoffencecode><recordableonpncindicator><code>Y</code><description>Yes</description></recordableonpncindicator><pncacpooffencecode>4.1.84.1</pncacpooffencecode><notifiabl